        "root_concepts": "[linux]",
        "section": "os",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "03 - Linux OS: Developer Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**The key mental shift from Windows**: There is no registry, no COM object model, no Win32 API surface. Everything — config, hardware access, process info, kernel parameters — is exposed as files in a tree. You read `/proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward` to see a kernel setting; you write `1` to it to enable IP forwarding. This is the \"everything is a file\" philosophy in practice."
    },
